  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Description",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The Schedule has a display switch called Business Hours. It is meant to grey out the parts of the day the shop is not open, so that a planner can see at a glance which part of the row is real working time and which part is the middle of the night.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The switch does nothing you can see. With it turned on, the whole timeline from midnight through to eleven at night is the same flat white as the working day, so a shift placed at three in the morning looks exactly as normal as one placed at ten in the morning.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It matters because this is the only cue on the board that tells a planner where the working day begins and ends. Without it, out-of-hours work is invisible until somebody notices the time and questions it, and the switch itself looks broken because turning it on and off changes nothing on screen.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Branch / Environment",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Application: https://sv8685.qa.shopview.com",
           "type": "text"
