        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Signed in as admin@shopview.com (Administrator)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Observed: 2026-08-06, 03:0x UTC",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Steps to reproduce",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Sign in as a user who can view the schedule (an Administrator is fine) and pick the location Staging Heavy Duty - 9919.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Open Schedule from the top navigation.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Switch to Day view using the Day / Week / Month control, and go to Thursday, 6 August 2026. Any day behaves the same way; the fault does not depend on the date or on any particular work order, technician or shift, and no test data is needed to see it.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Open the FILTER & DISPLAY dropdown in the toolbar and find the Business Hours switch. It is already on, which is its default.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Look along the timeline from 12 AM through to 11 PM.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Turn the Business Hours switch off, look again, then turn it back on and look a third time.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "orderedList"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Expected behaviour",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "With the switch on, the hours outside the working day should be covered by a grey overlay so they are visibly different from the working part of the day.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The Schedule specification asks for exactly that, in two places:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": "\"With the toggle on, the hours OUTSIDE the working day are shaded with a grey overlay.\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Governing requirement: Schedule specification, Confluence page 713031682, version 23, section 9 (Business Hours) and section 4.8 (Business-hours shading).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Current behaviour",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "With the switch ON, the timeline from 12 AM to 11 PM renders uniformly white. Nothing is shaded, tinted or bordered.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "With the switch OFF, the timeline looks identical.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "With the switch turned back ON, the timeline still looks identical.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "The only shaded element anywhere in the calendar in all three states is the divider between the department groups, which is unrelated to the time of day.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Images",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "No screenshot is attached. The finding was taken by reading the rendered page directly and was confirmed on a screen capture at the time, and the check is a single glance at the timeline, so an image adds nothing a reader cannot see immediately by following the steps.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Technical details for developers",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Measured with the toggle ON, OFF and restored to ON. In each of the three states the count of elements carrying the shaded cell class was the same:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Elements matching fc-cell-shaded: 2 in all three states. Both are the resource-timeline divider (class fc-resource-timeline-divider fc-cell-shaded), which separates the department groups; neither is a time-of-day overlay.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "No element in the Day-view time grid carries any non-working-hours class, background tint or overlay in any of the three states.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Confirmed visually on the captured screenshot, not only by class name.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is not the same as the two nearby reports, and a duplicate search was run before filing:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "SV-8827 is about the switch's DEFAULT STATE (it starts on when it should start off). This report is about the switch having no visible effect at all, whichever way it is set.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "SV-8837 and SV-8915 are about where the view is scrolled to when it opens. This report is about the shading of the hours once you are looking at them.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    }
   ],
